## 1. The Big Idea

_One sentence: **The face you've been perfecting for three articles is one small district of a much larger plot — and the jaw, where your whole routine quietly stops, is an arbitrary line that aging ignores; the poster must make the reader feel, instantly, that the dense care-hatching of the entire prior series dead-ends at the jaw while the sun pours straight across it onto the neck and hands that betray their age first, then read the rest of the body as a zoned survey where each region gets matched to its own fix — and the single cheapest win on the whole drawing is just running the line down.**_

The poster has to land three beats in one read: **the boundary** (a hard line at the jaw where "maintained" stops and "neglected" begins), **the betrayal** (the one warm photoaging vector that crosses the abandoned line freely and lights up the neck + hands — the 1.1 "~80%" thesis made literal, "the hands are the proof"), and **the territory** (the body below as a zoned map, each region tagged with its issue and its body-specific fix, kept deliberately lean).

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure — the hero object

**A WHOLE-BODY ZONING SITE-SURVEY: a single human figure drawn as an architect's front elevation / plot map, divided by a hard horizontal JAW LINE into an over-maintained FACE DISTRICT above and a neglected BODY TERRITORY below — with the dense "care" hatching of the entire prior Skin series stopping dead at that line, while one warm photoaging vector crosses it unobstructed and lights the NECK + BACKS-OF-HANDS as the betrayal zones, and the body below mapped into labeled gland-behaviour zones each carrying its own fix.** This is the anchor; nothing replaces it. The body is drawn as what the series has always called skin — *substrate, barrier, structure, plot* — so "survey," "zone," "district," "boundary line," "run the line down" render as architecture without forcing, and the dermal scaffold texture is a direct callback to 1.1.

This is deliberately the **zoom-OUT** of the track: 1.1 was one wall section, 2.0 the day run across it, 2.1 the cut behind it — **3.0 pulls the camera all the way back to the whole structure.** The eye enters at the bright, busy face, hits the jaw line, and is pushed *down* into the quiet neglected territory — the composition itself teaches *"you stopped here; keep going."*

- **THE FACE DISTRICT (top, above the jaw line — small, over-tended).** Drawn dense: tight maintenance hatching, a little cluster of the prior-series instruments ghosted in (the 1.1 wall-section, the 2.0 coat-schedule, the 2.1 gate-valve), captioned `EVERYTHING YOU'VE BUILT SO FAR — applied to one district.` It should read as *crowded with care* — almost comically well-tended next to what's below. A small slug: `the face = a different organ than the body. you optimized the small one.`

- **THE JAW LINE (the hero device — a hard horizontal boundary across the figure).** A bold, dashed **survey boundary line** ruled straight across at the jaw, labeled on the drawing edge `CARE STOPS HERE ▸ aging doesn't`. The dense face-hatching **butts up against this line and stops dead** — below it, the linework goes sparse, ghosted, unfinished, like a plot surveyed but never built on. This single line is the article's whole argument; if you see one thing in a thumbnail, you see the maintained district ending at a ruled line with the rest of the body trailing off below it. Rendered in the cool **slate instrument register** (it is a *measurement / boundary*, not a hazard — never alarm-red itself).

- **THE BETRAYAL — neck + backs-of-hands (the one warm photoaging vector crossing the line).** Carried verbatim from 1.1: a single **warm-red photoaging / UV vector** (the *only* place the dominant 80% force appears) that **crosses the jaw line unobstructed** — because sunscreen stopped at the jaw but the sun didn't — and pools on the **NECK** and the **BACKS OF THE HANDS**, drawn as the figure's oldest-looking, most-crepey zones. Caption clipped to these zones: `chronically sun-exposed + routine-neglected = age shows FIRST and WORST here. the hands are the proof of the ~80% (cf. 1.1).` The fix tag sits right beside it, almost insultingly cheap: `the entire fix → run SPF + retinoid + moisturizer DOWN past the jaw. nearly free.` This warm vector + these two lit zones are **rationed red mark #1.**

- **THE BODY TERRITORY (below the jaw — the zoned survey, the bulk of the frame).** The figure's body mapped into labeled **gland-behaviour zones**, each a small dimensioned callout matching *region → issue → body-specific fix* (this is where OTC doses are allowed to print, per house rule):
  - **BACK / CHEST / SHOULDERS — `OILY ZONE · "bacne."`** Two-branch callout: `(a) bacterial/hormonal → benzoyl-peroxide wash · salicylic · (± 2.1 systemic)` vs `(b) FUNGAL — Malassezia folliculitis → antifungal, NOT acne tx`. A short bracket beneath: `90% here = SWEAT HYGIENE — shower post-gym · breathable fabric.` The fungal branch is the home of **rationed red mark #2** (see interlock below).
  - **FOREARMS / UPPER ARMS — `DRY ZONE · keratosis pilaris ("chicken skin").`** `benign keratin plugging · MANAGE don't cure → urea 10–20% / lactic / salicylic lotion · gentle exfoliation · moisturize.` A small warm caveat tick: `don't scrub raw.`
  - **SHINS / LOWER LEGS — `DRY ZONE · flaking / eczema-prone.`** `urea + moisturize · gentlest washing.`
  - **TORSO / GENERAL — `the lean body routine.`** A compact stack tag: `BODY RETINOID PM (tone·texture·KP·photoaging, body-grade, same ramp rules) · UREA = the moisturizer workhorse · SPF on exposed zones (the bit everyone skips).`
  - **ABDOMEN / FLANKS / THIGHS — `stretch-mark survey`** (the closing-window device, below).

- **THE FUNGAL-ACNE INTERLOCK (rationed red mark #2).** On the back/chest zone, a small boxed **"WRONG-TREATMENT" trap** — the exact twin of Skin 2.0's fungal-acne trap and the harm-on-bypass red the series rations red *to*: `Malassezia ≠ bacterial acne. BP / actives FAIL (oils & esters can FEED it) → needs antifungal (ketoconazole / zinc-pyrithione). the tropical payload.` This is the only zone where treating the wrong cause makes it *worse*, so it earns alarm-red; every other body caution stays amber.

- **THE STRETCH-MARK CLOSING WINDOW (the verdict device — amber, not red).** A small horizontal sub-survey on the flank/thigh zone, read left→right as a closing window (cousin of Hair 1.1's condemnation line, kept *amber* to preserve the two-red discipline): `STRIAE RUBRAE (red/early) — a WINDOW · respond somewhat → retinoid · (2.1 microneedling/laser)` → a hard vertical line → `STRIAE ALBAE (white/mature) — window CLOSED · largely permanent → manage, don't promise.` Caption: `tell the truth: the red ones have a window, the white ones don't.`

- **THE MINIMUM-ROUTINE FOOTER (the anti-over-build grace note).** A short slate spec strip closing the frame: `THE BODY'S 90% = SUN + SWEAT HYGIENE + MOISTURIZE. don't over-build.` followed by the five-step minimum as a lean line: `gentle wash → urea/moisturize → SPF exposed skin → BP/antifungal wash as needed → optional body retinoid PM.` Deliberately drawn *smaller and simpler* than 2.0's elaborate face schedule — the contrast is the point: the body needs less, not a second full stack.

- **THE DEFERRED-SCOPE TAGS (boundary device, ghosted at the edge).** At the bottom edge, a faint cross-link fence: `cellulite / crepey / loose skin after fat-loss = mostly structural / fat-distribution → /fit body-composition (cf. 1.1).` Present so the reader knows the series sees it; deliberately outside this cut.

**The two-register surface (the signature move, reused).** Everything **above the jaw line is the "maintained register"** — dense, crisp, over-instrumented. Everything **below is the "neglected / surveyed-not-built register"** — sparse, ghosted, waiting for the line to be run down into it. The **two reds are the "fault register"** — the warm UV vector lighting the betrayed neck/hands, and the fungal trap on the back. The surface itself teaches *maintained vs neglected vs harmful* before a word is read.

Why this metaphor fits and nothing else does: the article's literal structure is *one over-tended region (face)*, *a hard behavioural boundary (the jaw)*, *betrayal border-zones that age first (neck/hands)*, *a zoned body territory (oily back, dry arms/shins)*, *one wrong-treatment trap (fungal)*, *one closing-window verdict (stretch marks)*, and *a deliberately lean minimum routine.* A whole-body zoning site-survey split by the jaw line is the only object that holds all of them at once and stays true to the capstone's job — *the wide shot that says "you forgot the rest of you."* A grid of "body products," a glowing full-body before/after, or a generic anatomical chart would flatten the boundary, bury the betrayal, and teach none of the zone-matching.

